@1 = ~You do not belong here. The depth are meant for Converted.~
@2 = ~What do you mean 'Converted'?~
@3 = ~Who are you and what happened to your skin?~
@4 = ~Is there anything I can do to help you?~
@5 = ~I think I'll leave you as you are...~
@6 = ~We are the Converted. I only begun the trails of great Schlumpscha - our saviour. He is chosen by Ghaunadaur, god of abominations, oozes and outcasts. He took us as his children, his servants - witnesses to his lifestyle. He made us HIS.~
@7 = ~What else do you want?~
@8 = ~What do you mean 'Converted'?~
@9 = ~Who are you and what happened to your skin?~
@10 = ~Is there anything I can do to help you?~
@11 = ~I think I'll leave you as you are...~
@12 = ~My real name has been forgotten by time... my new title is... Converted. I once roamed the streets of this filthy city you call Baldur's Gate. Now, I am home. After so long, I am home. This... is the gift of Ghaundanaur. He can bestow the same upon you, if you let him.~
@13 = ~What else do you want?~
@14 = ~What do you mean 'Converted'?~
@15 = ~Who are you and what happened to your skin?~
@16 = ~Is there anything I can do to help you?~
@17 = ~I think I'll leave you as you are...~
@18 = ~Help? Why help? I don't need any help. I am blessed, as are all children of the slime lord. I am honoured to be among the few of us. You cannot revert the process of purification. I, however, can grant you the privilege of becoming one of us.~
@19 = ~What else do you want?~
@20 = ~What do you mean 'Converted'?~
@21 = ~Who are you and what happened to your skin?~
@22 = ~Is there anything I can do to help you?~
@23 = ~I think I'll leave you as you are...~
@24 = ~You do that, child of Bhaal. Walk your own path if you are unwilling to accept ours.~
@25 = ~Wait, what did you say? How do you know?~
@26 = ~You shouldn't have said that. You know too much, and I don't like that. Time to exterminate the pest.~
@27 = ~Hehehehe. Startled, aren't we? Our chosen one - Schlumpscha granted his most devoted kin with knowledge. Years he spent in Candlekeep paid off. If he only hadn't...~
@28 = ~Hadn't what?~
@29 = ~Nothing. I spoke too much. Go. Walk away.~
@30 = ~There is no penance for non-believers.~
@31 = ~Poor fool. He accepted a bargain with a dangerous deity that cares none about his devotees. Ghaunadaur will swallow you whole and openly show his apathy over his pain and suffering.~
@32 = ~Ghaunadaur. Before Lolth rose to absolute dominance, Ghaunadaur was widely worshipped by the drow. Look at you, wallowing in the mud, singing praises to a literal puddle of slime. You survived the strictures of poverty just to lose your mind to an aberration? Pathetic.~
@33 = ~Mayhaps I shouldn't but I feel pity for this man. His mind is utterly lost with no way of reparation.~
@34 = ~Tiax fears no gods. Once Tiax becomes what he's destined to, he'll crush your slime god and swallow it whole. M... maybe not that last part.~
@35 = ~Only you could take us to a literal dumphole like this, <CHARNAME>. Look at my boots! They're ruined!~
@36 = ~By Tymora's grace! Mixed emotions are flowing through my mind right now. I'm hesitant to determine which one is stronger.~
@37 = ~If there's any more doubt why I find beggars and scroungers repulsive, here you go.~
@38 = ~Hideous, despicable caricature of a man. You're even more gross than a common peasant. It's beneath me to even stand in your presence.~
@39 = ~Boo does not like this man one bit. He reeks of death and evil, just like this whole place. Although I do think that kicking his butt would be unnecessarily cruel of us to do, since he's in... that state.~
@40 = ~I have goosebumps just looking at him. I really want to leave this place, <CHARNAME>.~
@41 = ~One more word from your dirty mouth and I shall reinvent your insides, you scum.~
@42 = ~Continue talking, you aberration, and I shall demonstrate what a purification truly means.~
